(Penske Automotive Group, Inc. \(NYSE: PAG\) faces structural vulnerability in its proposed take-private transaction by Motown Acquisition) Tj
T* (Corp. \(64% Penske Corporation, 36% Mitsui & Co.\). The transaction relies on a bifurcated stockholder approval structure where the Kahn v.) Tj
T* (M&F Worldwide Corp. \(MFW\) minority cleansing prong is contractually defined as 'a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested) Tj
T* (stockholders \(as defined in Section 144 of the DGCL\)' rather than a majority of all outstanding unaffiliated shares. This votes-cast) Tj
T* (formulation creates an identifiable litigation target under Delaware Chancery Court entire fairness jurisprudence, compounded by an 8.6%) Tj
T* (premium over the pre-announcement unaffected price \($212.00 cash vs. $210.00 initial bid, $195.21 unaffected baseline\). Concurrently,) Tj
T* (closing is conditioned on securing complex OEM change-of-control consents across global franchise networks and executing debt) Tj
T* (backstops for a $502.7M mandatory 101% par Change-of-Control Put on PAG's 3.75% Senior Subordinated Notes due 2029.) Tj
